65
00:09:45,454 --> 00:09:52,804
In the smartphone software, the goal is to analyze the spectrum and detect if there is a screen.

66
00:09:53,120 --> 00:10:10,052
And there are three components: the PA effect modeling, which try to understand the charge and discharge process of pin junction once facing the light, and a discharge pattern recognition and a screen detection algorithm.

67
00:10:11,054 --> 00:10:14,916
So, first, let's look at the PN effect modeling.

68
00:10:15,182 --> 00:10:20,196
We know when the P in junction is in front of a lighting source, it's gonna get charged.

69
00:10:20,814 --> 00:10:25,764
And here is the formula to model the charging process.

70
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:33,540
And we're gonna model the voltage and in real time and the time to charge and discharge.

71
00:10:34,446 --> 00:10:49,760
After we get the measure of the pin junction, the voltage on the pin junctions, we're gonna analyze the data to detect there is uh uh specific features related to the screen exposure.

72
00:10:50,062 --> 00:11:07,588
Particularly, we're gonna extract the signals in the discharge part and compare it and then use a template-based approach and see if there is a possibility to uh impose to a screen.

